+# dsh-side patches
+
+These are the DeepSeek Harness changes the skill hub still needs to reach its
+documented surface through **official extension points instead of DOM patches
+and private-service reads**. They are requests against the official harness, not
+vendored forks: each file applies to a `deepseek-harness` checkout with
+`git apply` and touches disjoint packages.
+
+Both are written against tag `dsh-v0.2.1-alpha.2` (the harness release this
+plugin was reviewed against; each also applies to the `dsh-v0.1.7-alpha.1` shape
+of the same files). Neither is upstream as of that tag.
+
+| Patch | Capability it serves | Why an official extension point is not enough |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| [`settings-nav-icon-seat.patch`](settings-nav-icon-seat.patch) | The **Settings → 技能** nav row wears the skill glyph (`src/client/settings-nav-icon.ts`). | The settings shell renders nav glyphs from a hard-coded `navIcon(id)` map and `settings.section` carries no icon option, so the plugin otherwise falls back to a `MutationObserver` DOM swap. The patch declares the keyed `settings.nav.icon` seat (declared by the shell, rendered with the built-in glyph as fallback), so a section registrant supplies its own glyph; the plugin already registers into that seat when the host declares it. |
+| [`input-trigger-source-lookup.patch`](input-trigger-source-lookup.patch) | The chat **`/` menu skill dots** (`src/client/slash-dots.tsx`), colored from the same config as the panel legend. | The dots already ride the official `InputTriggerCandidate.icon` component field, but reaching the core `/skill` source to attach them is not official: `ctx.inputTriggers` publishes only `registerSource`/`sessionOf`, so the plugin reads the service's private `live.sources` roster. The patch publishes `source(trigger, name)`, which removes the private read entirely. |
+
+Both requests already have upstream discussion threads:
+
+- nav glyph: [#2827](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/2827) (English feature request), [#2864](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/2864) (same request in Chinese; a maintainer reply proposes a validated icon token on `settings.section` **and** "a controlled icon render slot" for plugins that draw their own glyph — this patch is that seat), [#3022](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/3022) (plugins passing `icon:` today and getting the gear).
+- trigger source read: [#2878](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/2878) (closed; the registration side shipped as `registerSource`, no read side), [#2741](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/2741), [#6721](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/6721), [#2657](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/2657).
+
+Discussion drafts for both live in `.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/`:
+
+- `.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/settings-nav-icon-seat/report.md`
+- `.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/input-trigger-source-lookup/report.md`
+
+## Applying
+
+From the root of a `deepseek-harness` checkout at `dsh-v0.2.1-alpha.2`:
+
+```sh
+git apply /path/to/dsh-skill-hub/patches/settings-nav-icon-seat.patch
+git apply /path/to/dsh-skill-hub/patches/input-trigger-source-lookup.patch
+```
+
+Each patch carries the package README/subsystem-doc edits the harness requires
+next to the behavior change. Verify with the affected packages' own suites
+(`packages/client/ui-settings-general/tests`, `packages/client/ui-input-trigger/tests`).
+
+## Fallbacks on unpatched hosts
+
+Neither patch is required for the plugin to load or for a documented capability
+to work today. On a host without them the plugin keeps its degrade paths — the
+scoped DOM gear swap instead of the seat contribution (the plugin registers into
+`settings.nav.icon` whenever the host declares it), and the catalog-derived dots
+attached through the private roster instead of the public lookup. The degrade
+paths are not permission to drop the capabilities; they are how the surfaces
+survive missing extension points, and the patches are what retire them.
